== 6. what this does to the speed budget ==
  nominal crouch needs a 16.03 mm per-pair body shift, 0.4938 s
    not overlapped -> 0.01833 m/s
    overlapped with lower+dwell+load -> 0.02179 m/s
  aligned crouch residual offset 0.0464 mm -> no per-pair shift needed
    speed stays at the frozen ideal ceiling 0.02624 m/s
    the 0.0262 m/s ceiling and its asymptote v_peak/3.75 are unchanged; posture removes the statics penalty, not the timing limit

== 7. does the continuous lateral body motion undo the alignment? ==
  pure +y body motion projects onto the diagonal normal with factor 0.6412
  one pair swing lasts 1.1431 s and the body travels 30.00 mm laterally at the 60 mm step
    start aligned, drift one full swing              peak offset  19.24 mm  vs 12.42 mm  EXCEEDS CAPACITY
    bias so the COM crosses the diagonal at mid swing peak offset   9.62 mm  vs 12.42 mm  OK
  with the mid-swing bias, statics allows steps up to 77.5 mm, looser than the 60 mm landing cap: statics stops being the binding constraint
  margin at the 60 mm landing cap: 23%

== 8. what the sealed landing law actually does to that phase ==
  step  30.0 mm (v 0.01895 m/s, T_pair 0.7916 s): COM lateral offset from the support pair runs   -6.89 ->   +8.11 mm, peak perpendicular  5.20 mm  OK
  step  28.2 mm (v 0.01830 m/s, T_pair 0.7705 s): COM lateral offset from the support pair runs   -7.04 ->   +7.06 mm, peak perpendicular  4.53 mm  OK
  step  40.0 mm (v 0.02201 m/s, T_pair 0.9087 s): COM lateral offset from the support pair runs   -5.42 ->  +14.58 mm, peak perpendicular  9.35 mm  OK
  step  60.0 mm (v 0.02624 m/s, T_pair 1.1431 s): COM lateral offset from the support pair runs   -0.31 ->  +29.69 mm, peak perpendicular 19.04 mm  EXCEEDS
  the frozen constants centre the drift only at lead = 1.5*T_pair, i.e. T_pair 0.7700 s
    that is a 28.2 mm step and only 0.01829 m/s
  at the 60 mm cap the lead constant would have to be 1.5347 s instead of 0.975 s (total lead 1.7147 s = 1.5*T_pair)
    then the offset runs -15.00 -> +15.00 mm, peak perpendicular 9.62 mm, margin 23%
  note: T_pair depends on the projected step, which depends on the lead, so a corrected law needs a one-step fixed point or the previous pair period
  KEEPING the frozen 0.975 s lead, statics caps the step at 46.7 mm and the speed at 0.02365 m/s
    that is a third binding constraint, tighter than both the 60 mm landing cap and the 0.02624 m/s timing ceiling

== 9. can longitudinal acceleration substitute for the posture fix? ==
  moment arm of a body x-acceleration about the diagonal: 0.2974 m
  to cover 8.07 N*m needs 0.5634 m/s^2 held for the whole 1.0231 s air phase
    that would travel 294.9 mm, against the frozen 30 mm longitudinal excursion limit
  the limit only affords 0.0573 m/s^2 -> 0.82 N*m, 10.2% of what is needed
  so wheel-driven longitudinal acceleration cannot replace the posture fix; the required moment has one sign for the whole swing and cannot be oscillated
